# Superpowers Routing

Use installed Superpowers skills as the primary workflow layer. [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) defines priority when skills conflict with project policy.

## Skill routing

| User intent | Required flow |
|-------------|----------------|
| New feature / behavior / architecture change | `brainstorming` first → spec in `docs/superpowers/specs/` |
| Approved design or spec exists | `writing-plans` → plan in `docs/superpowers/plans/` |
| Plan exists; implementation starts | `executing-plans` or `subagent-driven-development` |
| Bug / regression / failing test | `systematic-debugging` |
| Any code change | `test-driven-development` discipline where practical |
| Review requested | `requesting-code-review` |
| Implementation complete | `finishing-a-development-branch` |

## Rules

- Do not skip design/spec/planning gates for non-trivial work.
- If the user says design is already approved, locate the spec/plan file before coding.
- Persona briefings run **immediately before** implementation; they do not replace brainstorming or writing-plans.
- Do not modify Superpowers plugin/skills source in this repo.
